   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Yes, we have access to the shiny server (currently installed on LInux OS) and have technical resources available to install nginx/Apache and configure mySQL user permissions.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Any issues with using iframes and bootstrap together?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Would it be possible with proxying to have journal pages and shiny visualizations residing on a separate servers, but both accessed from the same root URL? E.g., <a href=\"http://psesv.psfmc.org/index.php\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://psesv.psfmc.org/index.php&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388165935000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0gjaTkQXyH23jnA9BCeB_M\">psesv.psfmc.org/index.php</a> is the journal home page URL, and <a href=\"http://psesv.psmfc.org/PSESV1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://psesv.psmfc.org/PSESV1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388165935000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Nq7z6tlLJ0SOV9AWlAIKg\">psesv.psmfc.org/PSESV1</a> is the page for a shiny visualization.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
